<title>UK: UK index-linked bond tranche due 2006 exhausted.</title>
<headline>UK index-linked bond tranche due 2006 exhausted.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said a 150 million stg tap offer of 2.0 percent index-linked stock due 2006 was exhausted and no longer operating as a tranchette after the bonds were supplied finally at 185.24.  </p>
<p>The tranche was one of two tap stocks announced on August 29.</p>
<p>The other, a 200 million stg tranche of 2.5 percent index-linked gilts due 2020 has not yet been sold out.</p>
